    "type": "int",
    "min": 50,
    "max": 20000,
    "default": 2000
   },
   "tau": {
    "type": "float",
    "min": 1e-12,
    "max": 0.001,
    "default": 1e-08
   },
   "tau_spread": {
    "type": "float",
    "min": 1.2,
    "max": 10.0,
    "default": 2.0
   },
   "perturb": {
    "type": "float",
    "min": 0.0,
    "max": 0.01,
    "default": 0.0
   },
   "lr": {
    "type": "float",
    "min": 1e-09,
    "max": 0.001,
    "default": 1e-06
   },
   "beta0": {
    "type": "float",
    "min": 1000.0,
    "max": 100000000.0,
    "default": 100000.0
   },
   "beta1": {
    "type": "float",
    "min": 100000.0,
    "max": 100000000000.0,
    "default": 100000000.0
   },
   "cycle": {
    "type": "int",
    "min": 100,
    "max": 100000,
    "default": 2000
   }
  },
  "out": "runs/autocorr1",
  "log": "runs/autocorr1/{id}.log",
  "notes": "Minimize C (record 1.502743486709583 by Atris; a new record needs <= 1.5027434767). Starts from public solution --start (0 = record), np.repeat-upsampled by --upsample (exactly the same C), and resumes from the best best_*.json in --out with the same n. method=proxlin: prox-linear (sequential LP) descent on the max of the autoconvolution, dual FISTA with FFTs, --batch trust-region sizes in parallel, monotone. method=lse: annealed log-sum-exp + Adam (found no descent from the record in tests). Log lines: [autocorr1 s<seed>] t=..s best=<C> gap_to_top=<C - record> outer=.. tau=.. gain=..; negative gap_to_top means below the record, FOUND needs gap <= -1e-8 and is written only after the official O(n^2) verifier confirms. Measured on a shared A100: about -3e-10 in 2 min then ~1e-11 per 5 s and slowing; upsample 1 and 2 gave the same gains, upsample 1 is 2x faster. More --inner (5000-10000) gives larger gain per outer step at the same wall rate. One GPU, <2 GB memory, so several can share a GPU."
 },
