  "notes": "Polisher for the d=12, n=842 overlap penalty (minImprovement 0): block sequential LP with trust region on the EXACT hinge (scipy HiGHS, 40-point blocks), plus basin hopping (perturb, Adam on the softplus hinge annealed to exact, block-LP polish). Re-scored with the verifier's Decimal arithmetic on near pairs; FOUND only from the official verifier. Measured: the kgrey top (0.5309634950279605) admits no first-order descent in ~1500 block LPs, and removing its ~1240 tiny (~6e-12) contact overlaps by restoration makes it WORSE (+6.4e-9), so it is a genuine local optimum; basin hopping (tau 1e-6->1e-11, sigma<=1e-5) returns to 0.5309763, i.e. 1.3e-5 above it, in 4-min tests. HONEST: a lower positive penalty is a leaderboard improvement only, NOT a new kissing configuration (that needs penalty exactly 0). Odds: very low. Log: [polish_k12 s<seed>] t=..s best=.. record=.. gap=..; artifact runs/polish_k12/best_<id>.json"
 },
